2 CONT Itzcoatl (Classical Nahuatl: Itzcōhuātl /it͡sˈkoːwaːt͡ɬ/, "Obsidian Serpent") was the fourth emperor of the Aztecs, ruling from 1427 (or 1428) to 1440, the period when the Mexica[1] threw off the domination of the Tepanecs and lai
2 CONC d the foundations for the eventual Aztec Empire.
