1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was an adopted son of Simon Perez de Bustillo and his wife, Juana de Zamora. A mestizo, he was a natural son of one of Simon's sisters or of Simon’s with an Indian woman.  In 1642 he declared that he was related
2 CONC  to Nicolas Ortiz, brother-in-law, on his father's side.  He played a brief and tragic political role that ended in 1643. Along with his double uncle, Antonio Baca and his cousins, he was beheaded in 1643 for the assassination of 
2 CONC New Mexico Governor Rosas. 
