1 OCCU Bondsman for assassin Nicolas Ortiz in 1642. Alcalde of Canon de Jemez until 1662.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Miguel acted as bondsman for Nicolas Ortiz, assassin of New Mexico Governor, Luis Rosas.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Miguel de Hinojos, son of Fernando, held the Alcaldía of Jémez until Governor Mendizábal took it from him prior to 1663. He acted as bondsman for Nicolás Ortiz in 1642. Miguel also owned lands on the Santa Fe River about a league 
2 CONC south of the Villa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Origins of New Mexico Families, pg. 48
2 CONT
2 CONT Miguel married Zuni Woman about 1635 in Zuni Pueblo, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España. (Zuni Woman was born in 1621 in Zuni Pueblo, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España.
2 CONT --------------------
