2 CONT
2 CONT Doña Ana Moreno de Lara, married to Cristóbal Baca, absent for five year in passage to this district. She has two daughters who live with her named Juana, eighteen, and Luisa, seventeen. Likewise, she stated that she has two sons 
2 CONC who are absent, one named Francisco, who is married and lives at the Cosihuiriáchic mines, and the other named Felipe Baca, likewise married and living at the real of Parral. She has in this household two orphans named Felipe, fiv
2 CONC e, and Elena, twelve. I (Vargas) was also shown a granddaughter named Josefa, five.
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal Crown Restored, pg. 62
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT # EVENT: member '93 Varg: 4 OCT 1693 [3421] [3422] 
2 CONT
2 CONT [3421] Vargas noted that she was married to Cristóbal Baca, who had been absent for five years. Chávez assumes that Baca was dead by 1687, but Ana did not seem to consider him dead in December of 1692 when she chose to report him 
2 CONC as missing. It appears that he abandoned her for Gregoria de Luna in 1684. Her household contained two daughters, Juana, age18, and Luisa, age 17. There were two orphans and one granddaughter, named Josefa. The orphans were Felipe
2 CONC , age five and Elena, age twelve. Her absent sons were Francisco, married and living at the Cosihuiriáchic mines and Felipe, married and living at the real de Parral. Vargas reported that he was also shown a granddaughter named Jo
2 CONC sefa, age 5.
2 CONT
