1 NOTE Luisa /Rodas Lozano/
2 CONT In that city's protocol records of Miguel de Vargas, volume 10 and beginning in folio 240, dated 2 November 1738 is the will of Mariana Casillas y Cabrera.  Her legitimate parents were Francisco Casillas y Cabrera and Luisa Lozano
2 CONC .  A "vecina de esta ciudad" her death record's not in Los Altos.  "y mi entierro en la Santa Iglesia Catedral en la bóveda que pertenece a los Casillas, por ser legítima descendiente yo de ellos"
2 CONT
2 CONT Alonso Galván de Rojas married twice, to two women who were related, so a relationship by affinity required a "dispensa."  I don't have the document; it's long gone, but the fourth to the third degree blood relationship between h
2 CONC is spouses was in this manner:
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Juan López de Jimena md. Francisca de Nava
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Juan López de Nava			1st  (brothers)		Andrés López
2 CONT 	md. Inés López Muñiz						md. Isabel Ramírez
2 CONT 		|								|
2 CONT 	Ines López de Nava			2nd (first cousins)	Luis López Ramírez
2 CONT 	md. Hernando de Villegas					md. Catalina Rubio
2 CONT 		|								|
2 CONT 	Luisa de Rodas			3rd (second cousins)	Ana López Ramírez
2 CONT 	md. Fulgencio González de Ruvalcaba			(second spouse)
2 CONT 		|
2 CONT 	Luisa Rodas				4th
2 CONT 	(first spouse)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 ACTN 1519
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 ACTN F
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 ACTN 1519
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 ACTN F
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Surety:0
