1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptism [1]
2 CONT Juan, Spanish
2 CONT
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes, on the first day of August, one thousand six hundred and forty-seven years, I exorcised, catechized and baptized a child whom I named Juan, legitimate son of Joseph Delgado and Francisca Gavai. His g
2 CONC odfather, Juan Delgado, declared to them the relationship they had contracted. And for the record I signed it, ut supra .
2 CONT
2 CONT Bachelor Hernando Calderon
2 CONT Wedding [2]
2 CONT In the town of Aguascalientes in the parish church on four days in the month of March of one thousand six hundred and sixty-nine years, Mr. Bartolomé de Soto y Carvajal married and held a funeral service for Juan Delgado and Marga
2 CONC rita López de Lizardi, neighbors of this parish, Having preceded all the procedures established by the Holy Council and read three admonitions on three inter missarum solemnia holidays, which were Sunday the twenty-fourth of the m
2 CONC onth of February, and Friday the first, and Sunday the third of this month of March, and no impediment resulted, they were witnesses are Mr. Bernabé Altamirano, and Diego Gonzáles, and Gaspar Serrano and for the record I signed it
2 CONC  above.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bachelor Nicolás de Echerreaga
2 CONT
2 CONT July 16, 1732: Already deceased. [3]
2 CONT
