1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Josefa Lucero de Godoy''' aka Josepha Lucero de Godoi born c. 1642 at Nueva España
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no evidence that Josefa was married or had any children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josefa is the daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Sgto-major-Juan-Antonio-Lucero-de-Godoy/6000000008212796914 Sgto. major Juan Antonio Lucero de Godoy] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Do%C3%B1a-Luisa-Romero-de-Pedraza/60000000
2 CONC 00400805226?through=6000000008212796914 Doña Luisa Romero de Pedraza]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT She appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sixth household, two sons, two daughters, four dependents
2 CONT
2 CONT Sgto. major  Juan Lucero de Godoy, married to doña Isabel Hurtado de Salazar, states that his children are Matias, age thirty; Cayetano Lucero, age four; doña '''Josefa''', fifty; and Barbara, one.  He states that he has four depe
2 CONC ndents: Maria, Juana, Josefa, and Juan.  He states that he is a loyal vassal of his majesty, he is quite ready to enter with his family whenever I, the governor and captain general, enter to settle this kingdom.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kessell, John L. and Hendricks, Rick, editors, To The Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694, University of New Mexico Press. 1995, ISBN 0-8263-1559-3
