1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Josefa de Hinojos''' born c. 1662 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Diego-de-Montoya/6000000005599075599?through=6000000000401594371 Diego de Montoya, II]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Maria Josefa de Hinojos and Diego de Montoya, II:
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Montoya/6000000000401594355?through=6000000007528901004 Maria de la Rosa Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Juan-Montoya/6000000007529122154?through=6000000007529145667 Juan Esteban Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Lucia-de-Montoya/6000000007529153247?through=6000000007528901004 Lucia Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Antonio-Montoya/6000000007528901004?through=6000000007529122154 Antonio Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Salvador-Montoya/6000000007529145667 Salvador Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Juana-Montoya/6000000005599075537 Juana Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Miguel-Montoya/6000000000401594378?through=6000000005599075537 Miguel de la Cruz Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Montoya/6000000007529143039?through=6000000000401594378 Maria Isabel Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Marcial-Montoya/6000000007529142371?through=6000000007529143039 Marcial Montoya]
2 CONT #[http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Francisca-Montoya/6000000000401594371?through=6000000007529142371 Maria Francisca Montoya]
2 CONT
2 CONT Josefa is the daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/http://www.geni.com/people/Bartolome-DE-SALAZAR/4993361796590054440?through=6000000005599001861 Diego de Montoya, I] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-de-Hinojos/6000000005
2 CONC 599001854 Maria de Hinojos
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT After her father Bartolome de Salazar died, Diego de Trujillo took the three sisters, Marìa de Salazar Hurtado, Marìa Josefa de Hinojos and Isabel de Salazar Hurtado from their mother, Marìa de Hinojos, to be raised and adopted by
2 CONC  his granddaughter Bernardina Salas y Trujillo and her husband Andres Hurtado.
2 CONT
2 CONT She appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth household, three sons, three daughters, two servants
2 CONT
2 CONT Diego Montoya, regidor, married to '''Josefa de Hinojos''', with six children: Salvador, three; Juan Estevan, five; Antonio, three; Maria de la Rosa, eight; Luisa, four; Juana, two.  Likewise, this household has two married servan
2 CONC ts named Antonio and his wife, Ana Duran.  He states that, as a loyal vassal of his majesty, he is quite ready to enter to settle with his wife and children when I, the governor and captain general, enter.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kessell, John L. and Hendricks, Rick, editors, To The Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694, University of New Mexico Press. 1995, ISBN 0-8263-1559-3
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT kidnapped by Indians, rescued by Andres Hurtado; later adopted her along with his wife, Bernardina de Salas Orozco y Trujillo
2 CONT --------------------
