2 CONT Even though he was blind, he used his languge ability to warn of the impending Indian resistance that developed when Vargas was waiting for the Tanos to vacate Santa Fe. He had overheard the Indians talking about how they would de
2 CONC feat Vargas and informed Miguel Lujan who relayed the information to Vargas at 4 A.M. The fact that he was in Santa Fe in Dec of 1693 proves that he and his family made the trip north with the first reconquest settler party. The p
2 CONC hrase, 'his mother's tongue," seems to negate Fray Angelico's suggestion that he might have been Apache and supports the fact that his mother, Maria de Hinojos, was indeed pueblo (Zuni) .
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hgrc-nm.org/surnames/GNMPD.html/d0133/g0013353.html#I1238
