2 CONT '''''Augustin María de Salazar''''' '''''Born: 1665, Zuni Pueblo, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España''''' '''''Marriage: Felipa Teresa de Gamboa'''''  '''''Died: 7 Feb 1740, Santa Cruz de la Cañada, Santa Fé, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España at
2 CONC  age 75''''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''His name appeared on the Diego de Vargas El Paso Area Muster census from Dec 1692 to Jan 1693 in Pueblo la Ysleta del Sur, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España. P 287''''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Agustín de Salazar, married to Felipa de Gamboa, with two sons named Antonio, four and Miguel, two. Likewise, living in this house were his mother-in-law, named Lucía Martín, with one daughter, a young woman named Petrona Dom
2 CONC ínguez, sixteen. He states that being given a way to settle that kingdom, he will go with his family'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Dates & Events: 4 Oct 1693: He returned to New Mexico with Don Diego de Vargas in 1693.'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Dates & Events: He was an interpreter, "proficient in his mother's tongue." Even though he was blind, he used his languge ability to warn of the impending Indian resistance that developed when Vargas was waiting for the Tanos
2 CONC  to vacate Santa Fe. He had overheard the Indians talking about how they would defeat Vargas and informed Miguel Lujan who relayed the information to Vargas at 4 A.M. The fact that he was in Santa Fé in Dec of 1693 proves that he 
2 CONC and his family made the trip north with the first reconquest settler party. The phrase, 'his mother's tongue," seems to negate Fray Angélico's suggestion that he might have been Apache and supports the fact that his mother, María 
2 CONC de Hinojos, was indeed pueblo(or more appropriately, Zuni).'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Augustín and his wife Felipa de Gamboa had a daughter named Lugarda, who married Ficente Jirón in 1723. Another duaghter, Josefa, married Juan Lorenzo de Valdés. They also had a son anmed Antonio.''''' '''''~The Origins of Ne
2 CONC w México Families, P. 279'''''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''http://www.cybergata.com/roots/4865.htm'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''He had a residence in 1723 in Santa Cruz de la Cañada, Santa Fé, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España. P. 252''''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Augustin married Felipa Teresa de Gamboa, daughter of Juan de Gamboa and Lucia Martín Barba. (Felipa Teresa de Gamboa was born in 1672 in San Juan de los Caballeros, Santa Fé, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España 252 and died on 6 Feb 
2 CONC 1756 in San Juan de los Caballeros, Santa Fé, Nuevo Méjico, Nueva España 252.)''''' 
2 CONT
