1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carlos Cantú González, also known as Carlos Cantú y González Hidalgo, was born around 1705 in Puesto del Llano, in the valley of El Pilón (now Montemorelos, Nuevo León, Mexico). He was a prominent figure in the exp
2 CONC loration and colonization of northeastern Mexico, including regions like Nuevo Santander, Nueva Extremadura, and Nuevo Reino de León1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carlos was the eldest of eight siblings, born to Captain Carlos Cantú and Maria Josefa González. He married Ana Maria Gertrudis Cavazos de la Garza around 1730, and they had at least ten children2. Carlos played a significant role
2 CONC  in founding the city of Reynosa on March 14, 1749, and served as its first captain and chief justice1.
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away before 1767, but his contributions to the development of northeastern Mexico are well-remembered
