1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch ====
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicol%C3%A1s_de_Carvajal,_Marquis_of_Sarri%C3%A1 English - '''Wikipedia....''']
2 CONT * Nicolás de Carvajal y Lancaster, Marquis of Sarriá (died March 4, 1770) was a Spanish noble and military figure from the 18th century.
2 CONT * He was the son of '''Bernardino de Carvajal y Vivero''', second count de la Quinta de la Enjarada, and  '''Maria Josefa de Lancaster y Noroña'''. His mother was a descendant of Jorge de Lancastre, a natural  son of King John II 
2 CONC of Portugal. His brothers were José de Carvajal y Lancáster, Spanish prime minister between 1746 and 1754, and Juan Carvajal y Lancaster, 4th Duke of Abrantes.
2 CONT * He was lieutenant general, and colonel of the Spanish infantery regiment of the Reales Guardias. King Fernando VI made him a Grandee of Spain first class in 1755.
2 CONT * In 1762 he became commander of the Spanish invasion of Portugal, but he was very slow in assembling his troops and commencing the hostilities. This gave the British the time to bring over an expeditionary force in support of the
2 CONC  weak Portuguese army. King Charles III of Spain was disgusted by Sarria's lethargy and had him replaced by the Count of Aranda.
2 CONT * Sarria received  the '''order of the Golden Fleece''', as compensation, and as a reward for his earlier services to the Crown.
2 CONT * He '''married''' Ana María Josefa López de Zúñiga y Castro, marquesa de Sarriá, daughter of Juan Manuel de Zúñiga, 11the Duke of Béjar and Rafaela de Castro y Centurión, and widow of Ginés Miguel Fernando Ruíz de Castro y Portug
2 CONC al, 11th count of Lemos.
2 CONT * He '''died''' without an heir on March 4, 1770.
2 CONT ====Source====
2 CONT *  Vida de Carlos III. Tomo II p3 (in Spanish)
2 CONT * Grandes de España
2 CONT * Geneall.net
