1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Juan Cresostimo de Ulibarri, II''' named after his adoptive father, Apache birth name is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan was an Apache Indian who, as a child, was adopted and raised by Juan de Ulibarri and Juana Hurtado de Salas.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan de Ulibarri, Apache of unknown parents, married Rosalia Armijo, coyote daughter of unknown parents” on July 7, 1732. Witnesses: Juan Gonzales and Casilda Gonzales. [AM NMG XXI:3 p. 51]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rosalia Duran de Armijo (Marques) was the real daughter of Jose Duran de Armijo and Maria Manuela Velasquez, but she was given to Antonio de Ulibarri and Maria Duran y Chaves to raise as an adopted daughter because they could not 
2 CONC have children. [Origins of New Mexico Families Chavez, 1992 p. 300] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rosalia sued for her adoptive mother's inheritance in 1732. [SANM I, #236, 1732].
2 CONT
2 CONT An April 21, 1733 document entitled “Petitions of some half-breed Ind ians (genizaros) of various tribes, who had abandoned their tribal relations, to settle at the deserted pueblo of Sandia; denied by Governor Cruzat y Gongora”, 
2 CONC listed “Juan de Uribarri, Apache; married to Rosa; has a son.” [SANM I #1208, 1733]
2 CONT
2 CONT Juan be Ulibarri and Rosa Armijo were godparents of Feliciana Baca "Spanish" daughter of unknown parents, bt. Mar 2, 1749 [AB p. 64].
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 81 of the 1750 Census, Albuquerque, contains the following information: Juan de Ulibarri, Indian, 60 (DOB 1690); wife Rosalia Armijo, Spanish, 40 (DOB 1710); three children: Pedro Chrisostomo 16 (DOB 1734), Juana 15 (DOB 1735
2 CONC ), Joachim 8 (DOB 1742); two orphans, Andres 7, Bernarda 6, and Juana Maria, Indian 6.
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 4, 1756 murio Juan de Urivarri (in margin - Juan Urribarr, genizaro) de nacion Jenisaro, resivio todos los sacramentos y se enterro en esta Sta Yglesia, de 60 anos, casado con Rosalia de Armijo. [LDS 016645 Albuq. Burials
2 CONC  1727-1854]
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 3 of the 1790 Census, Albuquerque, contains the following information: Antonio Lopez, Coyote, 24 (DOB 1766), spinner, m. Maria Ysabel Pacheco, Coyote, 19; his mother, Juana Ulibarri, Mestiza, 50, widow; her son 15; her daught
2 CONC er 13; his grandmother Rosalia Marquez, Mestiza, 90, widow.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==BURIAL==
2 CONT El 4 de abril 1756 murio Juan de Urivarri //Juan Urribarr, genizaro de nacion Jenisaro resivio todos los sacramentos y se enterro en esta Sta Yglesia de 60 años, casado con Rosalia de Armijo [Source: LDS 016645 Albuq. Burials 1727
2 CONC -1854)
