1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Matías Luján and Francisca Romero, parents of Juana Luján #1, were in the area of San Ildefonso by 1701 when they were padrinos for Indian child baptized at San Ildefonso on 18 December 1701, and for another Indian child baptized 
2 CONC 2 February 1704 at San Ildefonso. In addition, Francisca Romero was also a madrina for another Indan child baptized at San Ildefonso on 10 Jaunuary 1703, and for an orhpan girl baptized 25 March 1703, San Ildefonso. Juana Luján wa
2 CONC s in the San Ildefonso area as early as 6 October 1703 when she was a madrina with Baltazar de Matha for an Indian girl. She was also a madrina for two other Indian children baptized at San Ildefonso on 5 December 1703 and 11 May 
2 CONC 1704. Among the marriage records of San Ildefonso Mission are the following records: Juana Luján and Gabriel Cabrera were padrinos for Bartolomé Lobato and Juana Carillo who were married at San Ildefonso on 21 August 1714; she and
2 CONC  José Trujillo, el mozo, were padrinos for Gerónimo de Ortega and Sebastiana de Jesús who were married at San Ildefonso on 9 July 1715. This Juana Luján is known to have purchased land near San Ildefonso Pueblo in 1714, and was la
2 CONC ter married with Francisco Martín (ONMF: 187).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://pages.prodigy.net/bluemountain1/bonmf4.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/110326636/person/120144310222 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 3 2017, 21:16:41 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT
2 CONT @R-1262306719@  Ancestry Family Trees  Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com.  Original data:  Family Tree files submitted by Ancestry members. 
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT Ancestry Family Tree  http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=39806366&pid=3036 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT When María Luján, widow of Pedro Sánchez de Iñigo, recorded her last will and testament on 13 December 1734, she declared that during the course of their marriage they had a total of eleven children and were named in this order: A
2 CONC ntonia, Manuela, Antonio, María, Olaya, Joseph [José], Juana, Lugarda, Figenia [Efigenia], Francisca Xaviela [Francisca Xaviera], and Xptoval [Cristóbal].
2 CONT
2 CONT Of these children, only Lugarda was deceased at the time when the will was recorded. She also mentioned that her husband was deceased. María Luján gave the following possessions to her children:
2 CONT A crucifix from Michoacán to Cristóbal.
2 CONT
2 CONT A painting of San Pedro to Francisca Xaviela.
2 CONT
2 CONT A small painting of San Isidro to Juana.
2 CONT
2 CONT A copper jar for drinking water and an iron roaster to Figenia.
2 CONT
2 CONT A "colchon escoplo y asuela," the iron brand, and a door from the bedroom to Joseph.
2 CONT
2 CONT The window and "una fresada Blanca" to Francisca Xaviela.
