1 NAME Juan Andrés /Archuleta/
2 GIVN Juan Andrés
2 SURN Archuleta
2 _MARNM Archuleta
2 NICK Mr. Juan Andres Archuleta
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1682
2 ADDR
3 CITY El Paso del Norte
3 STAE Provincia de Nuevo México
3 CTRY Reino de Nueva España
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1733
2 ADDR
3 CITY Santa Fé
3 STAE Provincia de Nuevo México
3 CTRY Reino de Nueva España
1 BURI
2 DATE 15 NOV 1733
2 ADDR
3 STAE NM
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Alfarez
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Andrés de Archuleta, son of Juan de Archuleta and Isabel Gonzáles, was an Alférez already in 1715. He was a member of Conquistadora Confraternity after 1700, in Santa Fé. He and his wife, Josefa Martín, were sponso
2 CONC rs for a child in 1713. In 1711, he was thirty-one years old, and therefore older than his brother Diego.
2 CONT
2 CONT His known children were Juan, Hilario and Asencio, the latter's name harking back to the first Archuleta of 1598. Evidentally there was also a natural son, Juan Antonio.
2 CONT
2 CONT ONMF, pg. 132
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
