1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Martina Lucero de Godoy''' born c. 1677 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martina Lucero de Godoy is the daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Antonio-Lucero-de-Godoy/6000000005598867328?through=6000000001015063084 Juan Antonio Lucero de Godoy, II] and [http://www.geni.com/people/Maria-Varela-Perea-Lo
2 CONC sada/6000000005598872177?through=6000000005598867328 Maria Antonia Varela Perea Losada]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT She appeared on the Don Diego de Vargas census 22 Dec 1692 to 2 Jan 1693 in El Paso del Norte, Nuevo Méjico. Nueva España.
2 CONT
2 CONT Third household, three sons, two daughters, two sisters, one orphan girl
2 CONT
2 CONT Adjutant Antonio Lucero, regidor, married to Maria Antonia Varela de Perea, with three sons and two daughters: Antonio, five; Juan, three; Diego, one; '''Martina''', fifteen; Bernardina, seven; two sisters, the one a widow named G
2 CONC eronima, without children, and the other, Maria, eighteen; and an orphan girl, eleven.
2 CONT
2 CONT To The Royal Crown Restored, pg. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Kessell, John L. and Hendricks, Rick, editors, To The Crown Restored, The Journals of Don Diego de Vargas, New Mexico, 1692-1694, University of New Mexico Press. 1995, ISBN 0-8263-1559-3
