1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marriage dispensation [1]
2 CONT Aguascalientes, March 26, 1720: Felipe Jaime, Spanish, [he said he was twenty-five years old] resident of this jurisdiction in the Jaltomate post, legitimate son of Jorge Jaime, deceased, and María Delgado, I appear to your worshi
2 CONC p in the best so that there is a place in law and I say that to better serve God our Lord I have tried and arranged to contract a marriage according to the order [of] Our Holy Mother Church with María de Medina, Spanish, [she said
2 CONC  she was eighteen years old] neighbor of this jurisdiction in the position of Santa María la Redonda, legitimate daughter of Juan de Medina and Teresa Díaz, deceased, and since the two are related by blood in the fourth degree
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses: Felipe Díaz, a Spaniard, resident of this jurisdiction, said he was forty years old; Cristóbal de Medina, a Spaniard, resident of this jurisdiction, said he was fifty-two years old; José Calvillo, a Spaniard, resident o
2 CONC f this town, said he was fifty-one years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2º	Margarita Lopez	cousins	Maria of Avila
2 CONT 3º	Maria Delgado	second cousins	Juan de Medina
2 CONT 4º	Felipe Jaime , would-be	fourth grade with	María de Medina , pretense
2 CONT
2 CONT May 16, 1767: Already deceased. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fuentes
