2 DATE 18 APR 1761
2 ADDR
3 CITY Alburquerque
3 STAE Provincia de Nuevo México
3 CTRY Reino de Nueva España
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Antonio Gurulé, born about 1703, was the only child of Santiago Gurulé and Elena Gallegos. At the age of 18, he married Antonia Quintana, the 16-year old daughter of Jose Quintana and Antonia Lujan Dominguez. Anton
2 CONC io was a farmer, and lived his whole life on the land grant property. The 1750 census of the Villa of Albuquerque, New Mexico, shows Antonio and his wife, six of their children, and two Indian servants (Rosa and Bernardina) and th
2 CONC eir children. Many of the Indian families who assumed the Gurulé surname were the children of Rosa and Bernardina. Nine children were born to Antonio and Antonia, and all are named in Antonio’s will of 1761. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.gurulefamily.org
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Antonio Grolet:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gurulefamily.org/ancestry/antonio.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT 1750 - NM, Villa de Albuquerque
2 CONT
2 CONT Antonio Gurulé (Spanish, 1705, age 45), Antonia Quintana (Spanish, 1705, age 45), Juan Antonio (1733, age 17), Fabiana (1734, age 16), Seraphin (1739, age 11), Elena (1741, age 9), Francisca (1743, age 7), Manuela (1746, age 4); s
2 CONC ervant: Rosa (Indian, 1710, age 40), Juan (1732, age 18), Juan (1738, age 12), Antonio (1742, age 8), Mathias (1744, age 6), Tomas (1746, age 4); Servant: Bernardina (Indian, 1720, age 30), Maria Antonia (1734, age 16), Ygnacio (1
2 CONC 739, age 11), Joseph (1741, age 9), Josepha (1744, age 6), Maria (1747, age 3)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.gurulefamily.org/resources/census/census_records.shtml
