1 CONT One of the original founders of Alburquerque.
1 CONT
1 CONT First called La Villa de San Francisco Xavier de Alburquerque, later changed to San Felipe de Alburguerque, it was founded as a Royal city by order of Don Francisco Cuervo y Valdez, Governor of New Mexico, on 7 Feb 1706. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Juan de Candelaria, most probably one of the original settlers, in 1776 when 84 years of age, wrote the first history of New Mexico. He states that it was settled by twelve families from Bernalillo with soldiers from that garrison
1 CONC . In his report to the Viceroy, Valdez reports that there were thirty families comprising the settlement. The only list we have is that given by Candelaria. There were more, as it is not probable that such a settlement would be ma
1 CONC de with so few.
0 @N6000000005024502541@ NOTE Catholic
0 @N6000000005024494725@ NOTE Catholic
