0 @N6000000005598904473@ NOTE Decendants of Sebastian and Ana Maria are listed on the Great New Mexico Surname Database and includes:
1 CONT
1 CONT - Juan Jose Duran- Abt 1720/ Aft 1760.  He married Felipa Trujillo on 19 Nov 1736 in NM.  They had Jose Maria, Margarita Rosalia, Jose Maria, Maria Barbara and Juan Jose Duran whose decendants are also listed.
1 CONT - Elena Duran- 1706 married Marcos Martin Serrano on 15 Sep 1723.
1 CONT - Salvador Duran- Abt 1710 married Juana Lujan on 26 Aug 1744 in San Juan DLC, NM
0 @N6000000005599062001@ NOTE Decendants of Diego and Juana are listed on the Great New Mexico Surname Database and includes:
1 CONT
1 CONT Maria Estela Marquez- Abt 1712.  She married Domingo Montes Vigil and they had Barbara, Francisco Antonio, Julian Montes, Gregorio Pablo, Nicolasa and Rosalia Montes Vigil.  Their decendants are also listed.
1 CONT Francisca Marquez- Abt 1710.  She married Pablo Manuel Trujillo on 8 Sep 1728 in Pojoaque, NM and they had Antonio Casimiro and Pablo Trujillo. Their decendants are also listed.
1 CONT Diego Antonio Marquez- Was baptized 15 Nov 1711, his padrinos were Nicolas Ortiz and Juana Ortiz.  He married Maria Gertrudis Esquibel on 25 Aug 1730 in Santa Fe, NM and they had Matheo Marquez, Ysabel Marquez and Juana Marquez.
0 @N6000000005599062040@ NOTE Decendants of Juan and Josefa are listed on the Great New Mexico Surname Database and includes:
1 CONT
1 CONT Maria Marquez- Born abt 1710 in Santa Fe, NM and baptized at the Military Chapel of La Castrense.  She married Andres Sandoval on 29 Jun 1728 in San Juan De Los Caballeros, NM.  Their decendants are also listed.
0 @N6000000002279616357@ NOTE MARIA TRUJILLO Y SANCHEZ:
1 CONT Juan de Trujillo and his wife, Elvira Sanchez Jimenez, both natives of the Rio Abajo, returned with the Reconquest....he was in all probability the Juan de Trujillo who passed muster in 1681, and the son of old Francisco Trujillo.
1 CONC ... His two know children were Maria, wife of Juan de Mestas Peralta, and Antonio, married to Ana Maria de Cordoba.
1 CONT Fray Angelico Chavez, Origins of New Mexico Families, Revised Edition 1992, p 296.
