0 @N6000000002279631704@ NOTE Don Lt. Felipe Romero of Joya, New Mexico
1 CONT Added by benedgar51 on 15 Mar 2008
1 CONT Source: Romero Family of Rawlins, Wyoming Tree
1 CONT
1 CONT The earliest document found regarding Felipe Romero is dated 20 July -September 3, 1733 in which he was involved in the proceedings of a lawsuit against Francisco Espejo regarding the sell of  2 horses.  This suit suggests that Fe
1 CONC lipe was of legal age in 1733 (21) therefore born prior to 1712.
1 CONT
1 CONT The earliest known record for Maria Casilda Mestas is 17 July 1744 when she acted as a sponsor with Nicolas Cisneros a child of Francis Xavier Mestas amd Teresa Vegil
1 CONT
1 CONT By March the pair are listed together as a couple in a document dated 2 March 1744 as sponsors of a child of Francisco Xavier Tafoya and Paula Martin. Wealthy or important people such as were the Dons and Donas were often expected
1 CONC  to act as sponsors not only for members of their own family but for other members of the community.  By the 1750's they were called upon to sponsor many of the children from families in the Santa Cruz are
1 CONT
1 CONT 21 Feb 1747 Casilda Mestas with Salvador Romero sponsored a child. It is possible that Salvador Romero is her brother-in-law. 
1 CONT
1 CONT 8 Jan 1749 Casild Mestas sponsored with Diego Romero a child. Salvador Romero de Padraza thought to be the father of Felipe did have a documented son named Diego born in 1689 which if the same would be 60 years old at this time.  
1 CONT
1 CONT 29 Jan 1749 Casilda Mestas sponsored with Salvador Romero a child
1 CONT
1 CONT 1 June 1751 Felipe Romero witness deed between Manuel Martin and Nicolas de Apodaca at Quemado, Rio Arriba with Juan Leon
1 CONT
1 CONT 20 Aug 1752 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Antonio Sandoval of Santa Cruz
1 CONT
1 CONT 17 June 1753 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Lazaro Trujillo
1 CONT
1 CONT 12 July 1753 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Juan Roque Cordova
1 CONT
1 CONT 30 July 1753 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Marcial Martin
1 CONT
1 CONT 25 June 1755 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Andres Trujillo
1 CONT
1 CONT 5 Aug 1755 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Nicolas Leal
1 CONT
1 CONT 22 October 1755 Felipe Romero sponsors a child of Capt. Juan Joseph Lavato
1 CONT
1 CONT 27 May 1756 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Juan Archuleta
1 CONT
1 CONT 5 Nov 1756 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Joseph Ricon
1 CONT
1 CONT 2 Feb 1757 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Joseph de Herrera
1 CONT
1 CONT 26 Feb 1757  Felipe Romero godfather of child of Bartolomew Martin
1 CONT
1 CONT 16 July 1757  Felipe Romero godfather of child of Francisco de Herrera and Francisca Mestas Santa Cruz
1 CONT
1 CONT 19 July 1758  Felipe Romerogodfather of child of Ynacio Pacheco Santa Cruz
1 CONT
1 CONT 2 Aug 1758 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Gabriel Ortega Santa Cruz
1 CONT
1 CONT 2 Feb 1759 Casilda Mesta sponsored with son Juan Miguel Romero a child at Santa Cruz
1 CONT
1 CONT 15 May 1760 Felipe Romero and Maria Casilda Mestas godparents for Vicente Romero
1 CONT
1 CONT 26 Jan 1766 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Bartholo Garduno Santa Cruz 
1 CONT
1 CONT Oct 1769 Felipe Romero godfather to child of  Cristobal Mascarenas
1 CONT
1 CONT 2 Feb 1770 Felipe Romero with daughter Maria Ynacia Romero god parents for child of Antonio Martin
1 CONT
1 CONT 18 Feb 1770 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Salvador Medina and Manuela Martin Santa Cruz 4 March 1770 Felipe Romero godfather of child of Salvador Romero Santa Cruz 
1 CONT
1 CONT 4 March 1770 Lt. Don Philipe Romero and Casilda Mestas godparents for Juana Geronima Romero daughter of Salvador Romero and Paula Mascarenas
1 CONT
1 CONT 25 March 1772 Felipe Romero with daughter Maria Ynacia Romero god parents for child of Alonzo Sandoval and Maria Rita Romero
1 CONT
1 CONT 16 May 1779 Felipe Romero with daughter in law Manuela Garcia godparents for child of Gervacio Duran and Victoria Sandoval
1 CONT
1 CONT 3 June 1779 baptismal record of Maria de Los Dolores Garcia daughter of Mariano Garcia and Antonia Sandoval list godparents “Juan Miguel Romero” and Manuela Garcia were sponsors.
1 CONT
1 CONT 12 December 1779 Felipe Romero and Casilda Mestas sponsored
1 CONT
1 CONT Documentation of Felipe Romero and Casilda Mestas are found in the 1750 census. 
1 CONT Spanish Census of the Villa Nueva de Santa Cruz de Canada 25 July 1750
1 CONT 197 Spanish families and 100 Indian families
1 CONT Phelipe ROMERO, his wife (Casilda Maesta) and 3 children (still at home)
1 CONT
1 CONT Nicholas ROMERO, wife (married Lugardo Valerio, Francisca Giltome y Lopez and Francisca Zamora) son of Francisco Xavier ROMERO)
1 CONT
1 CONT Bernardo ROMERO wife and 5 children (son of Francisco Xavier ROMERO)
1 CONT
1 CONT Juan ROMERO wife and 2 children
1 CONT
1 CONT Juan de Dios ROMERO wife (Maria Fernandez) , 3 children, 1 servent
1 CONT
1 CONT This census record clearly showed that Felipe Romero and Casilda Mesta had more children then what was recorded at Santa Cruz.
1 CONT
1 CONT Another document is a Will dated 20 Jan 1747 of Josefa Xavier Y Baca the wife of Luis Garcia de Noriega .  Luis Garcia de Noriega and Josefa Xavier Y Baca were married 27 August 1703. This will mentions a daughter Maria Rosa Garci
1 CONC a de Noriega wife of Ventura Romero.  A marriage record dated 4 February 1776 from San Juan de Los Caballeros shows a Lorenzo Romero  age 21 (1755) as the son of Buena Ventura Romero and Maria Rosa Garcia de Noriega.
1 CONT
1 CONT Lorenzo Romero married Maria Geronima Chaves y Lujan.
1 CONT
1 CONT Here is another Romero marrying imto the Garcia de Noriega family.  Ventura Romero may be a relative of Tomasa Romero, Salvador Romero, and Felipe Romero. A document dated 3 September 1767 through 19 January 1771 contains a lawsui
1 CONC t beteen Ventura Romero and Antonio Baca regarding some sheep.  Antonio Armijo is also a part of the suit
1 CONT
1 CONT A baptismal record from San Juan de Los Caballeros dated 22 October 1750 shows that Phelipe Romero and Casilda Maesta were the godparents to Salbador Feliciano de Jesus Lovato son of Captain Juan Joseph Lavoto and Elena Martin Ser
1 CONC rano.  Elena Martin was the daughter of Manuel Martin Serrano and his wife Elena Roybal. 
1 CONT
1 CONT On 1 June 1751 Manuel Martin granted to Nicolas de Apodeca land at San Francisco Xavier de Pueblo Quemado in Rio Arriba County, New Mexico about a league from Santa Fe and the document was witness by Felipe Romero. Manuel Martin w
1 CONC as uncle to the wife of  brother-in-law of Salvador Garcia de Noriega who would be the father-in-law of Jose Miguel Romero.
1 CONT
1 CONT  In a marriage inquiry 16 Feb 1779 to 12 March 1779 between Antonio Jose Romero and Maria Baca, a widow, records show that he was born 1743 the son of Felipe Romero and Casilda Mestas. The church was investigating whether the two 
1 CONC should be permitted to wed due to beling related in the "3rd and 4th degree of consanguity on a traverse line."  Felipe and Casilda were referred to as citizens and natives of Santa Fe.   While the record doesn't show how they are
1 CONC  related Maria Baca's mother was Teodora Fernandez de Pedraza. Felipe Romero's grandfather is thought to be Felipe Romero de Pedraza.
1 CONT
1 CONT Felipe Romero died before his wife who is found as a widow in the 1790 Census of San Juan.  There are no records found mentioning Felipe Romero after December 1779. He died probably in his 70's in the 1780's. Casilda Mestas is lis
1 CONC ted in the 1790 New Mexico Census as a widow some distance from Miguel Romero as household number 304. Miguel Romero is household number 50 leaving near his Garcia in-laws.
1 CONT
1 CONT The 1790 Census of San Juan shows the following:
1 CONT Casilda Mestas Spanish age 68 (1722) a widow
1 CONT Son age 18 (1772) and 1 female servent.
1 CONT
1 CONT If the census is correct Casilda was bearing children until she was 50. If Casilda Mestas first child was born when she was 21 she would have been considered an older mother also.  She had a son born in 1743.  Her husband Felipe R
1 CONC omero was at least ten years older than she.
1 CONT
1 CONT On 12 December 1779 Felipe Romero and Casilda Mestas acted as the sponsors for the son of Gregorio Martin and his wife Maria Victoria Tenorio.  The child was named Felipe de Jesus Rafael Martin and may have been named for his God 
1 CONC father Felipe Romero.  This baptismal record is evidence that Felipe Romero and his wife were residents of Joya in 1779.  Jose Miguel Romero would marry the following year to a girl from Joya. This baptismal record is the last doc
1 CONC ument located in which Felipe Romero is mentioned. He probably died between 1779 and 1783 when his wife was mentioned as a sponsor along with Jose Miguel Romero of the Comanche woman.
1 CONT
1 CONT Casilda Mestas probably married again after the 1790 Census for reords show that a Rafael Antonio Luna was married to a Casilda Mestas in 1791.
