0 @N6000000005024511226@ NOTE From "Beyond Origins of New Mexico Families", Volume 2: Gertrudis Cháves (ONMF: 163) wife of Francisco Silva (ONMF: 289) was not a daughter of Nicolás Durán y Cháves as documented in Origins of New Mexico Families by Fray Angelico
1 CONC  Chaves.  Prior to marriage, Nicolás had a son, Juan José by Juana Montaño.  While (he) was traveling out of New Mexico, Juana Montaño had given birth to a boy christened Nicolás and was pregnant with her third child, Gertrudis, w
1 CONC hen Nicolás return to New Mexico. Nicolás, the younger, and Gertrudis, natural children of Juana Montaño, were said to have been fathered by "a decent man named Urbán".  Nicolás Durán y Cháves was forced to marry Juana Montaño.  
1 CONT
1 CONT This information comes from the testimony of Antonio Cháves, half-brother of Gertrudis Cháves, given during the pre-marital investigation of José Manuel Silva and María Josefa Silveria Sánchez.
